  "reason": "Evidence: The two completed experiments (config_044 and config_004) show that avgpool aggregation (0.542) outperforms transformer (0.520) when paired with scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion in a multimodal multiprofile setup. However, the RNA encoder dimension is completely unexplored—only scgpt has been tested. Question: config_047 tests scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder while holding all other settings at their current best-known values (multimodal, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted). This is a clean single-variable ablation that will reveal whether a different RNA representation (variational autoencoder-based, 200-dim) can improve upon scgpt. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is a fundamental architectural choice that likely has a large impact on performance. With 7 experiments remaining, resolving whether scgpt is optimal or whether scvi_n200 offers gains is the highest-information experiment. If scvi_n200 matches or beats scgpt, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scgpt as the right encoder and lets us focus budget on other variables (image encoder, fusion, profile setting)."
